## SEO, Discoverability & Social Sharing (Universal)

Apply these rules to every public-facing page unless the user explicitly opts out (e.g. internal tools, staging-only apps).

### Goals & Scope
- Optimize for: **crawlability**, **correct indexing**, **rich link previews** (OG/Twitter), **Core Web Vitals**, and **semantic HTML**.
- SEO rules complement a11y and performance — never trade UX or security for rankings.
- Lighthouse SEO score is a **technical baseline**, not proof of search rankings.
- Do NOT keyword-stuff, use hidden text, cloaking, or misleading metadata.

### Project Setup (Single Source of Truth)
- Centralize site-wide SEO config in one module (e.g. `lib/seo-config.ts` or env):
  - `siteName`, `siteUrl` (`metadataBase`), default `title` template, default `description`
  - default OG image path, `locale`, `twitterHandle` (optional)
- Page-specific metadata overrides only what differs from defaults.
- Never put secrets, API keys, or admin credentials in metadata, README, or `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` vars.

### Metadata (Next.js App Router — adapt for other frameworks)
Every indexable public route MUST define:
- **`title`**: unique, descriptive, ≤ ~60 characters
- **`description`**: unique summary, ≤ ~155 characters, natural language (no keyword lists)
- **`metadataBase` / canonical URL**: absolute production URL; one canonical per page
- **`robots`**: `index, follow` for public pages; `noindex, nofollow` for admin, auth, API, staging, duplicates
- **Open Graph**: `title`, `description`, `url`, `type`, `locale`, `images[]`
- **Twitter Card**: `summary_large_image` (or appropriate card type), aligned with OG

For multi-page apps: no duplicate titles/descriptions; use title template (`"%s | SiteName"`).

### Social / Link Previews (Often More Important Than Google)
- Provide a default OG image: **1200×630 px**, optimized (< 300 KB), readable at thumbnail size.
- Page-specific OG images when content differs significantly (blog post, product, event).
- After OG changes, verify with a sharing debugger (Facebook, LinkedIn, or opengraph.xyz).

### Structured Data (JSON-LD)
- Emit JSON-LD from **server-rendered** HTML only (RSC, layout, page) — not from client-only components.
- Use schema types that match **visible page content** (Google policy: no mismatch between UI and schema).
- Common types by project:
  - **Marketing / SaaS**: `WebSite`, `Organization`, `SoftwareApplication` (if applicable)
  - **Blog / docs**: `Article`, `BreadcrumbList`, `FAQPage` (if FAQ visible on page)
  - **E-commerce**: `Product`, `Offer`, `BreadcrumbList`
  - **Events / bookings**: `Event`
  - **Local business**: `LocalBusiness`, `PostalAddress`
- Validate with [Google Rich Results Test](https://search.google.com/test/rich-results) when adding or changing schema.

### Crawling & Indexing
- Provide **`sitemap.xml`** listing only **indexable** public URLs (with `lastModified` when meaningful).
- Provide **`robots.txt`**: allow public routes; disallow `/admin`, `/api`, auth callbacks, internal tools.
- Use **`noindex`** on: login, dashboard, preview, thank-you pages (if duplicate content), search result pages with thin content.
- Register production domain in **Google Search Console** (and Bing Webmaster if relevant); submit sitemap after deploy.

### HTML Semantics & Content
- Exactly **one `<h1>`** per page; logical **`h2` → `h3`** hierarchy without skipping levels.
- Critical page content must be in **initial HTML** (SSR/RSC/static), not only after client hydration.
- Prefer Server Components / static generation for SEO-critical copy; isolate `"use client"` to interactive islands.
- Images: meaningful **`alt`** text; decorative images use `alt=""`.
- Links: descriptive anchor text or **`aria-label`** — avoid generic "click here" / "read more" without context.
- Set correct **`<html lang="...">`**; add **`hreflang`** only when multiple locales exist.

### Performance = SEO (Core Web Vitals)
- Targets (mobile): **LCP ≤ 2.5 s**, **CLS ≤ 0.1**, **INP ≤ 200 ms**.
- LCP element: optimize images (WebP/AVIF, responsive `sizes`, avoid multi-MB assets), prioritize above-the-fold media.
- Minimize render-blocking JS/CSS; lazy-load below-the-fold media and non-critical scripts.
- Do not claim "90+ Lighthouse" or "optimized CWV" without measured before/after evidence.

### Security & SEO
- Admin and API routes: **`noindex`** + auth; not linked from public sitemap.
- Canonical URLs prevent duplicate indexing (www vs non-www, trailing slash — pick one convention).
- Use HTTPS in production; `metadataBase` must use `https://`.

### Anti-Patterns (Never Do)
- Keyword stuffing in title, description, or invisible DOM
- Fake reviews/ratings in schema
- Schema for content not shown to users
- Indexing staging/preview environments
- Blocking CSS/JS in robots.txt (breaks rendering for Googlebot)

### AI Checklist Before Merging SEO-Related Changes
- [ ] Unique title + description for affected route(s)?
- [ ] `metadataBase` / canonical correct for environment?
- [ ] OG + Twitter tags + image present?
- [ ] JSON-LD matches visible content and validates?
- [ ] Sitemap / robots updated if routes changed?
- [ ] Admin/internal routes excluded from index?
- [ ] One h1, logical heading order?
- [ ] Indexable content server-rendered?
- [ ] LCP/image impact considered?
- [ ] No secrets in public metadata or docs?

